  "notes": "SOURCE: https://www.cartwheelsgymcentre.com/programs.php\nCartwheels Gym Centre - Programs About Programs Adapted Programs Registration Events Parties Contacts Cartwheels Programs Program Registration Schedule at a glance Tiny Gym (1 and walking to 3 years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> Your child's first gym class! This class is for our youngest gymnasts with their parent/caregiver. It focuses on both sensory and gross motor development, co-ordination, balance, strength, flexibility, social skills, and fun!! **The 1-year old participants are strongly recommended to be fully independently walking before the term begins. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 TUESDAY 9:15-10:00 10:15 - 11:00 4:00 - 4:45 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 WEDNESDAY 10:15 - 11:00 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 THURSDAY not scheduled SATURDAY 9:30 - 10:15 10:30 - 11:15 SUNDAY 8:30 - 9:15 9:30 - 10:15 10:30 - 11:15 --> Rock n' Roll with Miss Kelly (0+ years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> This class offers a safe environment for your child to grow physically, cognitively, and socially through music and movement. In this class we will use sensory rich props and musical instruments as we enjoy interactive playtime through song, dance, and physical literacy. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. Music Instructor - Platinum Music Instruction - Gold Tumble & Learn (2y 11m to 4 years) 2 hours $ per term --> Preschool & Kindergarten readiness program at Cartwheels. Tumble n’ Learn will focus on gross and fine motor development; sensory skills; strength, coordination, balance, and flexibility; independence and social skills. This two-hour drop-off program will include 45-minutes of a structured gymnastics class, music class, learning activity, group games, and a healthy snack break (nut/peanut free snack brought weekly by participants). This program allows participants to register for longer than one term length for increased development and continuity for the children Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. Mini Gym (3/3½ - 4 years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> Our eligibility rule for Mini Gym is that they have just participated in our Tiny Gym program (in the term prior to their move to Mini Gym) AND are showing signs of readiness to participate without a parent, OR are already 3 ½ when registering. If your child is new to Cartwheels, OR is a returning member with a break between participating in our terms, and they are not yet three years + six months prior to the term start date, they must register into Tiny Gym. This is to learn the routine, expectations, and structure of our program. No exceptions due to the demand & limited Mini Gym spots. **Participants must also be fully toilet trained (no pull-ups) to register into Mini Gym. If you choose to proceed with registration past the pop-up informing you of these requirements, you will be contacted to move to Tiny Gym or refund/credit your registration until they are eligible. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 5:15 - 6:00 TUESDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 4:00 - 4:45 WEDNESDAY 9:15 - 10:00 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 THURSDAY not scheduled SATURDAY 8:30 - 9:15 9:30 - 10:15 11:30 - 12:15 SUNDAY 10:30 - 11:15 --> Kindergym (4-6 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> A fast paced class geared to channel this age group's energy in a positive direction. This class provides opportunities to build social skills, self-confidence, and develop physical and motor attributes including: flexibility, strength, power, and endurance as well as balance and spatial orientation. All this in a gymnastics setting! Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 WEDNESDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY 8:30 - 9:20 9:30 - 10:20 10:30 - 11:20 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY 8:30 - 9:20 9:30 - 10:20 11:30 - 12:20 --> JR Gym (6-8 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY 5:00 - 5:50 WEDNESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 7:00 - 7:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY 10:30 - 11:20 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY 11:30 - 12:20 --> SR Gym (8-10 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 6:30 - 7:20 TUESDAY 7:00 - 7:50 WEDNESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 7:00-7:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 7:00 - 7:50 SATURDAY 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY not scheduled --> Preteen/Teen Gym (ages 10+) 60 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those over age 10 wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY not scheduled WEDNESDAY not scheduled THURSDAY 7:00 - 7:50 SATURDAY not scheduled SUNDAY not scheduled --> Cartwheels Plus Programming (5 years to teen) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> An invitation only advanced class open to those that need to be challenged at a higher level and can handle being taught at a faster rate than our other programming. This class will focus on strength and flexibility training as well as more advanced skills. Participants must be invited from Cartwheels programming and registration requires a code to unlock the program. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY not scheduled WEDNESDAY not scheduled THURSDAY 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY not scheduled SUNDAY not scheduled --> Ability Athletics Special Needs Programming - Social Sports - Playability - Movability Program Information Cartwheels Gym Centre &copy; Website by Nakoda Creative\n\nSOURCE: https://haltonhillsgymnastics.com/index.php/programs/recreational-programs/preschool-kinderfun\nPreschool & Kinderfun × Home Programs Recreational Preschool & Kinderfun Gymnastics Trampoline Tumbling Ninjas Drop-Ins Competitive Competitive Trampoline Parties/Camps Birthday Parties March Break Camp Summer Camps Kids' Nights at HHGC About Us About HHGC Our Difference Facilities Management & Staff Board of Directors Coaches Testimonials News HHGC News HHGC Apparel Shop HHGC Newsletter Parent Portal Contact Home Programs Recreational Preschool & Kinderfun Gymnastics Trampoline Tumbling Ninjas Drop-Ins Competitive Competitive Trampoline Parties/Camps Birthday Parties March Break Camp Summer Camps Kids' Nights at HHGC About Us About HHGC Our Difference Facilities Management & Staff Board of Directors Coaches Testimonials News HHGC News HHGC Apparel Shop HHGC Newsletter Parent Portal Contact Pre-school & Kinderfun Breadcrumbs Home Programs Recreational Preschool & Kinderfun Pre-School Drop-in under 4 yrs Cost: $15, one parent/up to 4 children. No pre-registration neccessary and payment can be made in person. Please note that we will numbers in the facility and this program is first come. Days and Times: Tuesday and Thursday 9:30 am - 12:00pm Drop In Begins September 15th and runs till June 26. (Closed Dec. 18 - Jan 5th, not running over March Break) Looking for a fun and safe place to hang out? Come bring your busy preschoo l aged child ( unde r 4 ) to one of our fun-filled drop ins! Parents will stay with their child while their child explores our gymnastics equipment. Bounce on the trampoline, swing on the bars, tumble down the cheese or jump in the pit. No experience necessary. Get involved and play with your kids in the best gymnasium in town. Please note that this program only runs during the school year (Sept- Jun) and follows the same schedule as our recreational programs. There is no drop-in outside of these dates. There is no Drop In on Statutory Holidays or March Break. Drop in is for Pre-school age children only. Kindergym: 3-5 Years Boys & Girls age 3 – 5 years. Kindergym is a fun-filled, structured program that improves balance, flexibility, strength and coordination through our progressive five level skill system that is both rewarding and challenging. This is a 55 min class. Fall 2026 Session 14 (13) weeks: September 12 - December 18 Winter 2027 Session 12 (11/10) weeks: January 2 - April 1 - Registration begins October 27th 12 weeks - Tues, Wed, Thur and Sat classes, 11 weeks - Mon, 10 weeks - Fri **Fees are pro rated for stat holidays where classes are not running ** No Classes March 13 - 19th March Break You never pay HST at HHGC! Advanced Kindergym Boys and Girls: 4-5 Years Advanced Kindergym Boys and Girls: 4-5 Years This is a program for the advanced kinder-gymnast who shows a keen interest and potential for gymnastics. They will learn more advanced basic gymnastic skills, spend more time on the equipment and focus on developing skills with the polish and presentation needed for further advanced gymnastics training. These gymnasts will be working on higher levels within the Kinder program. This program is for both boy & girl gymnasts! This is a 55 minute class for gymnasts aged 4-5 years. Prerequisites - Baby Cartwheel, Baby Bridges without support, Baby Handstands, Hangs on Bars, Balance on higher beam without help Fall 2026 Session 14 (13) weeks: September 12 - December 18 Winter 2027 Session 12 (11/10) weeks: January 2 - April 1 - Registration begins October 27th 12 weeks - Tues, Wed, Thur and Sat classes, 11 weeks - Mon, 10 weeks - Fri **Fees are pro rated for stat holidays where classes are not running ** No Classes March 13 - 19th March Break You never pay HST at HHGC! Parent and Tot 18 months - 3.11 yrs 18 months - 3.11 yrs. This program is for the toddler who loves to be on the move! This class involves parent participation and is led by a coach through a structured warm-up, games, music, and circuits on all gymnastic events. This is a 30 min. class. Fall 2026 Session 14 (13) weeks: September 12 - December 18 Winter 2027 Session 12 (11/10) weeks: January 2 - April 1 - Registration begins October 27th 12 weeks - Tues, Wed, Thur and Sat classes, 11 weeks - Mon, 10 weeks - Fri **Fees are pro rated for stat holidays where classes are not running ** No Classes March 13 - 19th March Break You never pay HST at HHGC! Aspire Group: Girls Aged 4-5 Years The Aspire Group will learn pre-developmental skills for the goal of moving toward the competitive program for female gymnasts. These gymnasts will spend more time on the equipment to work on advancing the skills they already have. Emphasis is put on strength, flexibility, and balance development. Gymnasts will start to become familiar with the Ontario Developmental Program (ODP). This is a 1 hour and 25 minute class for gymnasts aged 4-5 years. Prerequisite: This program is for children who have been recommended by a Coach or Manager demonstrated and have the ability to grasp the concepts of the fundamentals at a more accelerated rate, and have been in a gymnastics program for a minimum of 2 sessions and are ready for more challenges. More exercises to develop strength, co-ordination and flexibility in order to progress. At least 2 sessions prior to this class is a pre-requisite. Fall 2026 Session 14 (13) weeks: September 12 - December 18 Winter 2027 Session 12 (11/10) weeks: January 2 - April 1 - Registration begins October 27th 12 weeks - Tues, Wed, Thur and Sat classes, 11 weeks - Mon, 10 weeks - Fri **Fees are pro rated for stat holidays where classes are not running ** 